omer within the Apple Pay sheet, we return an NSError that can be displayed in the Apple Pay sheet.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Otherwise, the original error is returned, resulting in the Apple Pay sheet being dismissed. You should display the error message to the customer afterwards.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Currently, we convert billing address related errors into a PKPaymentError that helpfully points to the billing address field in the Apple Pay sheet.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Note that Apple Pay should prevent most card errors (e.g. invalid CVC, expired cards) when you add a card to the wallet.","type":"text"}],"title":"pkPaymentError(forStripeError:)"},"doc://com.stripe.stripe-apple-pay/documentation/StripeApplePay":{"type":"topic","role":"collection","title":"StripeApplePay","identifier":"doc:\/\/com.stripe.stripe-apple-pay\/documentation\/StripeApplePay","kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/stripeapplepay","abstract":[{"text":"StripeApplePay is a lightweight Apple Pay SDK intended for building App Clips or other size-constrained apps.","type":"text"}]}}}